course: dictionary
lesson: 2450
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «The Danes sailed across the sea and raided the monastery.» Here Danes means people from Denmark who lived long ago. The clues are sailed and raided, which are things that happen in history stories.
explain: «A Great Dane is huge but gentle and calm.» Here Dane is part of a dog's name. The two capital letters and the words huge and calm are your clues that this is about a dog, not a person. Ask yourself: is this about a person, a dog, or history?
explain: Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. «She spoke Danish at the party.» Danish means the language of Denmark, and it makes sense here. If your meaning does not fit, try the other meanings until one does.
fact: A Dane is a person from Denmark, and Danes is the word for more than one Dane.
fact: A Great Dane is a very large, tall dog, one of the tallest dogs in the world, and it is gentle despite its size.
fact: Long ago, the Danes were Vikings from Denmark who raided and settled in England and Ireland.
fact: The Danelaw was the part of England that was ruled by the Danes.
fact: Words like Dane, Danes and Danish start with a capital letter because they are names of people or a language.
exercise: «The Danes sailed across the sea and raided the monastery.» Who were the Danes? | Farmers who grew apples | *People from Denmark who were Vikings | A breed of very large dog | A kind of pastry from a bakery
exercise: «A Great Dane is huge but gentle and calm.» What is a Great Dane? | A kind of cake | A Viking ship | A person from Denmark | *A very large, tall dog
exercise: «She spoke Danish at the party.» What is Danish in this sentence? | *The language of Denmark | A giant dog | The name of a Viking king | A type of sea
test: «King Alfred fought the Danes and later made a deal with them.» Why are the Danes named here? | They were people who sold food at market | They were a breed of tall dog | *They were Vikings from Denmark who attacked England | They were teachers at a school
test: «A chihuahua and a Great Dane are the same species.» What does this sentence tell you? | A chihuahua is a kind of wolf | Dogs and wolves are different species with no link | A Great Dane is not a dog at all | *A chihuahua and a Great Dane are both dogs of one species
exam: «A big Great Dane standing on its back legs can be taller than a grown man.» Which meaning of Dane is used here? | A Viking king | A person from Denmark | A language | *A breed of dog
